1.	Publication is abstract as we have an abstract method inside
	the class. If we tried to instantiate Publication the program
	would throw a compiler error as abstract classes cannot
	be instantiated directly
	
2.	Book specializes Publication by adding, city, edition, isbn,
	and publisher variables. This is added to the title, and year
	variables already made by Publication.
	
3.	Polymorphism allows you to change how a method acts depending
	on the class its defined in. This is done by making publication
	abstract.

4.	Composition allows for the changing and replacing of components
	without affecting the min class. We do this for Citation, as
	we don't want our citation form to change.